      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "00c3c499-eac9-5e95-a2b1-6cdea470a0c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris DeStefano, Brett Eldredge, Carrie Underwood, Billy Currington, Luke Bryan, Miranda Lambert, Rascal Flatts, Jason Aldean, Terry Eldredge\n- Places: Mt. Laurel, New Jersey, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Songs: Good Girl, Little Toy Guns, Hey Girl, Don't Ya, That's My Kind of Night, Kick the Dust Up, Somethin' Bad, Rewind, Just Gettin' Started, Beat of the Music, Mean to Me, Drunk on Your Love\n- Albums: Bring You Back\n- Charts and Media: Billboard Country Airplay, NBC Sunday Night Football\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, record producer, multi-instrumentalist\n\nFacts:\n- Chris DeStefano is an American singer-songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist who was raised in Mt. Laurel, New Jersey, and resides in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- Chris DeStefano is a Grammy Award-winning artist.\n- Chris DeStefano wrote multiple No. 1 songs, including Carrie Underwood's \"Good Girl\" and \"Little Toy Guns.\"\n- Chris DeStefano wrote Billy Currington's \"Hey Girl\" and Brett Eldredge's \"Don't Ya\" as No. 1 songs.\n- Chris DeStefano wrote Luke Bryan's No. 1 songs \"That's My Kind of Night\" and \"Kick the Dust Up.\"\n- Chris DeStefano wrote \"Somethin' Bad\" for Miranda Lambert and Carrie Underwood, and that song was later reworked as the opening theme for NBC Sunday Night Football.\n- Chris DeStefano wrote Rascal Flatts' \"Rewind\" and Jason Aldean's \"Just Gettin' Started\" as No. 1 songs.\n- Brett Eldredge is the cousin of Terry Eldredge of The Grascals.\n- Brett Eldredge had three No. 1 singles on the Billboard Country Airplay chart from his debut studio album \"Bring You Back\": \"Don't Ya,\" \"Beat of the Music,\" and \"Mean to Me.\"\n- \"Drunk on Your Love\" is a song that Brett Eldredge co-wrote and recorded.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
